index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..fccc170311401a572967468432699528380b5a1f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/designs/numeric-conversion-normalization.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Canonical checked conversion normalization
+
+Named extraction disables only the pinned compiler's opportunistic small-body
+inlining. Explicit inlining remains enabled, including Option.bind. This keeps
+ordinary named helper closures in the established first-order subset; it does
+not recognize specialized names or admit runtime closures.
+
+Before type discovery and lowering, a single pass reconstructs closed, safe,
+total dictionary constants/projections used by checkedConvert. It checks their
+kernel types and definitionally compares source integer interpretation and the
+target minimum, maximum, and fromInt to the built-in scalar operations/ranges.
+It independently checks the actual operand and Option result types. Dictionary
+spelling is irrelevant. Open, altered, ill-typed, unsafe, or partial inputs are
+refused. A validated conversion retains only its scalar operand in LCNF; the
+existing typed checked-convert IR operation enforces target bounds.
+
+Backward liveness removes only the validated dictionary graph consumed by those
+calls and unused elsewhere. It retains other uses and unsupported generic type
+declarations. It must not perform generic dead-code elimination: a separately
+inserted unused bounded-Nat addition overflow is replayed as AddOverflow in
+native and Wasm generated code. Type discovery and body lowering receive the
+same normalized declaration, and coverage reports retained unsupported types.
+
+This is a local semantic argument about recognized closed dictionary fields,
+not a mechanized universal compiler-equivalence theorem or proof that entire
+numeric roots cannot fail. Existing generic Int/closure/array refusals and UOR
+guards remain in place. Compiler-owned fixtures are test inputs, not substituted
+application Lean or handwritten target implementations.
+
+The reconstructed candidate requires fresh pinned-SDK compilation, regression
+results, and independent review. See scripts/check-numeric-source-stage.sh for
+the full source-stage command contract; every failed gate remains recorded.
